From 78ac6d539b75e47e6799dea9a487333767ab0ce2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 10:10:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00812/11362] [outer-loop] Boosted 4-model judge panel: energy
 verifier DOMINATES all SOTA local judges

Full panel (n=528, internal GPU, conductor paused). Energy verifier AUROC 0.810
beats EVERY local SOTA judge at the strong 160tok/2048ctx budget AND is
9,232-16,036x cheaper (walltime):
  gemma-4-12B-it   judge 0.664  (best judge; 9,232x)
  Qwen3.6-35B-A3B  judge 0.640  (15,050x)
  gemma-4-31B-it   judge 0.488  (15,199x)
  gemma-4-26B-A4B  judge 0.449  (16,036x)

NUANCE (honest): boosting the token budget did NOT rescue all judges. With the
JUDGE prompt, gemma-4-26B stays ~0.449 even at 160 tok (vs exp3916's 0.663 which
used the SELF-VERIFY prompt on the same model) -- so prompt framing, not just
budget, drives the weak judges. Two of four (Qwen-35B, 12B) reach ~0.64-0.66.
Either way the energy verifier (0.810) dominates the whole panel on accuracy +
cost. Added a direct-llama fallback loader so gemma-4-12B (newly released; emits a
leading newline that trips the shared smoke gate) gets a fair real-prompt smoke.

DRAFT artifact; not conductor-wired. Follow-up: also test the self-verify prompt
framing as the judge to bound the strongest-prompt baseline.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
